# OI-037: transport-hardening security headers for Cloudflare Pages.
#
# This file lives in `public/` (Vite's default publicDir — unset in vite.config.ts,
# so it defaults to `public/`), which Vite copies verbatim to `dist/` on build.
# `wrangler.toml` sets `pages_build_output_dir = "./dist"`, and Cloudflare Pages
# reads a `_headers` file from the root of that build output — so this becomes
# `dist/_headers` at deploy time. See https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# CSP is shipped as Content-Security-Policy-REPORT-ONLY for this PR, not enforcing.
# Rationale: this environment cannot open a real browser to click through the live
# Pay Now flow (Stripe Elements iframe + redirect, Supabase auth) to confirm the
# policy doesn't break it. Report-Only ships the identical policy, reports would-be
# violations to the browser console (no report-to/report-uri configured — console
# only), and is inert to real traffic. Follow-up: after a manual browser
# verification pass against a deployed preview, flip the header name below to
# `Content-Security-Policy` (drop `-Report-Only`) to enforce.
#
# style-src: left under the default-src 'self' fallback (no 'unsafe-inline' added).
# React's style={{...}} prop (used in PortalPayNow.tsx and others) sets style
# properties via the CSSOM (node.style.prop = value), which CSP does not treat as
# an inline-style violation, and Tailwind v4 (@tailwindcss/vite) + @fontsource
# packages compile to a same-origin stylesheet, not inline.
# EXCEPTION (the earlier "no inline <style> tags" finding is stale): the shadcn
# ChartStyle in src/components/ui/chart.tsx injects a <style> element at runtime
# for chart color variables. Radix Dialog/Sheet scroll-lock and sonner may also
# inject <style> elements (UNVERIFIED - check the Report-Only console during the
# browser pass). Flipping to an enforcing CSP therefore needs a style-src decision
# first (e.g. style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline', or nonces). Chart bars carry a
# token fallback (var(--color-KEY, token)) so they are not black if that is blocked.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://js.stripe.com; connect-src 'self' https://api.stripe.com https://*.supabase.co; frame-src https://js.stripe.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
